<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Guelph Stormwater Basins &mdash; OSM Coverage Gaps</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../index.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="gaps.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="gaps.js"></script>
<script data-goatcounter="https://osm-guelph.goatcounter.com/count" async src="//gc.zgo.at/count.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Guelph stormwater basins &mdash; OSM coverage gaps</h1>
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; reference layer</a>
    <a class="back" href="history.html">gaps over time &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count missing"><strong>{{MISSING_COUNT}}</strong><span>basins missing in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count unclassified"><strong>{{UNCLASSIFIED_COUNT}}</strong><span>mapped as plain water</span></div>
    <div class="count creek_unnamed"><strong>{{CREEK_COUNT}}</strong><span>named creeks unnamed in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count wetland"><strong>{{WETLAND_COUNT}}</strong><span>constructed wetlands</span></div>
    <div class="count classified"><strong>{{CLASSIFIED_COUNT}}</strong><span>tagged as basins</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{CITY_COUNT}}</strong><span>City basins &middot; {{CREEKS_COUNT}} named creeks</span></div>
    <div class="count"><strong>{{OSM_COUNT}}</strong><span>OSM water areas</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">City data {{DATA_DATE}} &middot; OSM data {{OSM_DATE}} &middot; compared {{BUILD_DATE}}</div>
  </div>
  {{OSM_NOTE}}
  <details class="tagging">
    <summary>Which tag suits which basin</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Wet pond</strong> (a permanent pool): <code>natural=water</code> +
        <code>water=basin</code>, optionally <code>basin=retention</code> &mdash;
        the scheme Guelph's mapped ponds already use.</li>
      <li><strong>Dry basin</strong> (a grass hollow that floods after a storm):
        <code>landuse=basin</code> + <code>basin=detention</code>. It is not
        water most days, so not <code>natural=water</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Infiltration basin</strong>: <code>landuse=basin</code> +
        <code>basin=infiltration</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Constructed wetland</strong>: not settled &mdash; listed apart,
        nothing suggested.</li>
      <li>Either scheme counts as <em>tagged as a basin</em>; a bare
        <code>natural=water</code>, <code>water=pond</code> or
        <code>water=reservoir</code> counts as <em>plain water</em>.</li>
      <li>The City's <em>plan</em> is a subdivision-plan label, <strong>not a
        name</strong> &mdash; never copy it into <code>name</code>. A creek's
        City name is a real name: that is the one to add.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
  <p class="licence">
    <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">{{LICENSE_NOTICE}}</a>
    Sources: <a href="{{DATASET_PAGE}}">Stormwater Management Pond</a>,
    <a href="{{CREEKS_PAGE}}">Watercourse Polygons</a>.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="gap-map"
       data-geojson="gaps.geojson"
       data-raster="../tiles/raster/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label><span class="swatch missing"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-missing" checked> Missing</label>
        <label><span class="swatch unclassified"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-unclassified" checked> Plain water</label>
        <label><span class="swatch creek_unnamed"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-creek_unnamed" checked> Creek unnamed</label>
        <label><span class="swatch wetland"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-wetland"> Wetland</label>
        <label><span class="swatch classified"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-classified"> Tagged as basin</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by type, place, creek...">
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        Blue fills are the City's basins (raster layer); coloured dots flag the
        gaps. Click a row to outline it on the map, then press <kbd>O</kbd> to
        open it on openstreetmap.org or <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD editor (each row
        has the same <strong>OSM&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;iD</strong> link pair; for
        a mapped basin or a creek they open the OSM element). Matching is by
        spatial overlap &mdash; verify against imagery before editing OSM.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="gap-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th class="col-name">Basin or creek</th><th>Size</th>
              <th>Status</th><th>OSM now &rarr; suggested</th><th>OSM &middot; iD</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

</body>
</html>
